# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Kept deliberately in step with the "redirects" block in vercel.json — a rule
# that exists on one host and not the other silently disappears at cutover.
#
# Legacy contact URLs. Earlier drafts of the site (and a few externally linked
# variants) pointed at /contact-us, /support and friends. Serving those as a
# soft 404 through the SPA fallback leaves Google crawling dead variants and
# splitting the local-SEO signal that /contact is meant to own. A 301 passes
# the link equity across and gets the old URLs dropped from the index.
/contact-us          /contact   301
/contactus           /contact   301
/contact.html        /contact   301
/contact-support     /contact   301
/get-in-touch        /contact   301
/support             /contact   301
/help                /contact   301
/customer-service    /contact   301
/pages/contact       /contact   301
/contact/*           /contact   301

# SPA fallback must stay last so the rules above win.
/*                   /index.html   200
